  "meta": {
    "name": "PM C15 - finalize the BTS member delistings opened by C8",
    "description": "Completes the delisting of the 7 BTS members opened by C8 on 2026-07-20. C8 called requestDelisting, which only OPENS the 7-day wind-down window; nothing closes it. The window elapsed 2026-07-27 12:53 UTC and no finalizing transaction was ever sent, so all 7 have sat in DELISTING (status 6) for 41 days. Because pm-platform-api's subjects list shows every status except DELISTED (subjects-service.ts:311), they reappeared on the board the moment the indexer start block was corrected to cover their original listing. Phase 1 (tx 1-7) SubjectRegistry.forceSettle -> DELISTED. Permissionless and the window has long elapsed, but batched here so it is ordered before phase 2. Phase 2 (tx 8-14) PerpEngine.forceSettleSubject captures each subject's current on-chain mark, which is what a position holder would settle at. All 7 have ZERO open interest (longOI=0, shortOI=0 verified on chain), so phase 2 settles nothing today - it completes the lifecycle so no DELISTED subject is left without a settlement mark. Marks are read from PerpEngine.markOf at build time and are stale (the oracle has not pushed since early August); with zero OI that is economically irrelevant and every value is inside [MIN_MARK=1, MAX_MARK=1e36]. IRREVERSIBLE: DELISTED is terminal and forceSettleSubject reverts on a second call (SubjectAlreadyForceSettled).",
    "txBuilderVersion": "1.16.5",
    "createdFromSafeAddress": "0x1dfF78ED621fD37E495C6b5ef39D75a3e244651A"
  },
